Images used by the gw-ring part. Downloaded 2026-09-27.

ligo_hanford_aerial.jpg
  Aerial view of the LIGO Hanford Observatory, 2400x1600, unmodified file.
  Downloaded from: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LIGO_Hanford_aerial_05.jpg
  Original source (per Commons): LIGO Laboratory gallery,
    https://web.archive.org/web/20170614214509/http://www.ligo.org/multimedia/gallery/lho-images/Aerial5.jpg
  Author: LIGO Laboratory.
  Licence: Commons tags it {{PD-USGov}}. That tag is doubtful (LIGO Laboratory is run by
  Caltech and MIT, not by federal employees), so the slide relies on the LIGO image use
  policy instead (https://www.ligo.caltech.edu/page/image-use-policy, read 2026-09-27 via
  the Wayback Machine copy of 2024-01-01): LIGO images "may be used for any purpose without
  prior permission", with the credit line "Courtesy Caltech/MIT/LIGO Laboratory".
  Not checked: whether this exact photo also appears on a caltech.edu or mit.edu page, which
  is the scope that policy names.
  The slide shows the photo mirrored left-right (in part.js), so that the L is upright:
  corner station at the lower left, one arm to the right, one arm up. The slide carries
  the credit line "Photo: Courtesy Caltech/MIT/LIGO Laboratory (mirrored)".
